Initialize the I2C communication
Initialize with the Multiplexer (TCA9548A)
Initialize microcontroller (FireBeetle ESP32)
Initialize magnetic encoders (AS5600)
    -base
    -shoulder
    -elbow
    -wristYaw
    -wristPitch
    -wristRoll
Initialize slide potentiometer

Set channels for the econders on the Multiplexer
Set analog input pin for the potentiometer

Main Loop forever:
    For each joint (base, shoulder, elbow, wristYaw, wristPitch, wristRoll):
        Select Multiplexer channel for the joint
        Read the encoder angle
        Store the angle in an array of joint angles

    Read the potentiometer value for gripper
    Map the value to the gripper positions

    Display the joint angles and gripper value telemetry 

    Send joint angle and potentiometer values to the rover arm via CAN

    Wait some refresh rate amount of time

End Loop

